                <div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 20px;">
                    <!-- Group 1: General Concept -->
                    <div id="faq-group-general" class="faq-group-pane active-faq-group" style="background: rgba(15, 76, 129, 0.02); border: 1.5px solid var(--border-color); padding: 20px; border-radius: 6px;">
                        <h3 style="color: var(--accent-blue); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-color); padding-bottom: 8px; margin-bottom: 12px; font-family: Georgia, serif;">🌐 General Concept</h3>
                        
                        <div class="faq-item" style="border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-color); padding: 12px 0;">
                            <button class="faq-question" style="background: transparent; border: none; width: 100%; text-align: left; font-size: 1.05em; font-weight: bold; color: var(--text-primary); cursor: pointer; display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; padding: 5px 0; font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif;">
                                <span>Q: What is Cash-and-Carry Arbitrage?</span>
                                <span class="faq-icon" style="transition: transform 0.2s; font-size: 0.8em; color: var(--accent-blue);">▼</span>
                            </button>
                            <div class="faq-answer" style="max-height: 0; overflow: hidden; transition: max-height 0.2s ease-out; color: var(--text-secondary); font-size: 0.9em; line-height: 1.5;">
                                <p style="margin: 8px 0 0 0; padding-bottom: 10px;">
                                    Cash-and-carry is a market-neutral strategy where an investor buys an asset in the spot market (Cash) and simultaneously shorts it in the perpetual futures market (Carry). By maintaining a delta-neutral position (1:1), the investor is immune to price volatility and profits purely from the interest-like funding rates paid between long and short contract holders.
                                </p>
                            </div>
                        </div>

                        <div class="faq-item" style="border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-color); padding: 12px 0;">
                            <button class="faq-question" style="background: transparent; border: none; width: 100%; text-align: left; font-size: 1.05em; font-weight: bold; color: var(--text-primary); cursor: pointer; display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; padding: 5px 0; font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif;">
                                <span>Q: Why do we buy Spot and short Futures? (Why do we need Futures?)</span>
                                <span class="faq-icon" style="transition: transform 0.2s; font-size: 0.8em; color: var(--accent-blue);">▼</span>
                            </button>
                            <div class="faq-answer" style="max-height: 0; overflow: hidden; transition: max-height 0.2s ease-out; color: var(--text-secondary); font-size: 0.9em; line-height: 1.5;">
                                <p style="margin: 8px 0 0 0; padding-bottom: 10px;">
                                    Trading Spot allows us to buy the physical asset. Trading Futures allows us to short (hedge) the asset with leverage. By buying Spot and shorting Futures 1:1, our overall price risk is zero (Delta Neutral). If the coin price goes up, Spot profits offset Futures losses. If the coin price drops, Futures profits offset Spot losses. This allows us to safely harvest funding payments without price exposure.
                                </p>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                        
